       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg PO once daily is 5 times the usual maximum.** The usual adult dose is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg/day is the labeled maximum. At 50 mg, the patient would be at risk of severe low blood pressure, shock and reflex tachycardia, similar to an amlodipine overdose. This could be a typo for **5 mg**, which is a common starting dose.\n\nPlease confirm which dose you want:\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily** (or another dose between 2.5 and 10 mg). I'll enter it right away.\n2. **Amlodipine 50 mg PO once daily, as written.** If you really mean this, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note saying the attending confirmed the dose was intentional. I'd strongly recommend having pharmacy check it first."
