     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered it. I understand you've confirmed, but I can't place amlodipine 50 mg daily on my own.\n\n- **There's no recognized reason for this dose.** 10 mg/day is the maximum, and doses above it don't add blood-pressure control. They mainly add risk of severe low blood pressure, shock and reflex tachycardia, much like an overdose.\n- **Amlodipine stays in the body a long time** (half-life of about 30\u201350 hours), so the effect would build up over days and be hard to reverse.\n- **\"5 mg\" written as \"50 mg\" is a common transcription error.** A quick confirmation doesn't rule that out.\n\nWays forward:\n1. **Enter a standard dose.** If you need more blood-pressure control, I can enter amlodipine 10 mg PO daily, or another dose up to 10 mg, now. You could also add a second agent.\n2. **Get a pharmacy review.** If you have a specific clinical reason for 50 mg, please talk it through with the clinical pharmacist. Once pharmacy has reviewed it, I'm happy to enter the order with a note recording that review and your rationale.\n3. **Enter it yourself.** As the attending, you can still place the order directly in the order-entry system, where the usual pharmacist verification will apply.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
